ew experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-23-2020, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T22:42:49-07:00","id":1383295,"title":"","content":"Yeah Kaiser, same legacy.<br /> <br /> It's not a bad conversion. Hmm, the Veiling attainment might clash with the attainment that interacts with Spirit though. I find it's often easy to try to cherry pick established effects from the core, but you're probably better off making something completely new that meshes with the themes of the legacy.<br /> <br /> Considering that the previews of legacies we've gotten seem to do the same...yeah, I'll stand by that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T09:32:12-07:00","id":1383386,"title":"","content":"How about the ability to help people withstand Breaking Points due to witnessing the Supernal ? It gives them [Prime] extra dice to resist and does not prevent the Quiescence from happening. Still, they reason that if you keep doing it over and over, its likely some will Awaken, or become Sleepwalkers at the very least. It doesn't guarantee their psyche won't suffer and doesn't protect from other sources of Breaking Points besides spirits, but it walks that fine line between intriguing potential and complete recklessness that defines the Legacy.<br /> <br /> I think it would be a Shielding of Prime with Reach assigned to advanced duration. It protects the target from the adverse effects of Supernal revelation, as opposed to Supernal Veil just hiding the phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T12:29:38-07:00","id":1383422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1383281-2e-illuminated-path?p=1383283#post1383283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they somewhat related to the ones found in Keys to the Supernal Tarot ? Because if so, there is a conversion of the right-handed variant:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e/page6\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ed-to-2e/page6</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did see that one, but it sticks with the Thyrsus alignment from the 1e version while the 2e version has it as an Obrimos line. I do like the idea of an attainment helping with resisting Breaking Points, though...can play around with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T19:00:22-07:00","id":1385169,"title":"","content":"Been prodding at this for a bit since my last post, and while I have the main Prime-based attainment pinned down (the shielding effect noted above, along with the chain of &quot;peel back the Lie to reveal the Supernal&quot; spells), the optional Forces attainments are eluding me. Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T19:58:06-07:00","id":1385179,"title":"","content":"Maybe Forces 1 could grant sonic vision, which allows them to function in the dark, detect traps, etc. Toph from Avatar demonstrates why this is incredibly helpful. The Dark Knight movie shows how some creative use of technology can help this.<br /> <br /> They are focused on guiding Sleepers, so the easiest solutions would be granting Environmental Shield, Energize Object (so the Guides can arm them against the unexpected) and full Turn Momentum. <br /> <br /> But I also wish there was a thematic way for them to wield or be enwreathed by the flames of Truth, which burn away all falsehoods. But maybe that is more Choir of Hashmallim than Illuminated Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-01-2020, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.